## Goal
Perform a Principal Component Analysis (PCA) of the samples using gene expression counts, coloured by experimental condition, to visualize sample clustering and separation between groups.

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| counts_gene | 01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |
| design | 01_prepare_samplesheets | 01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv |

## Method
1. Run a Python script (`scripts/run_pca.py`) in the `gars-bio` environment.
2. Read gene counts from `02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv` and sample design from `01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv`.
3. Filter low-count genes, apply log2 transformation (log2(count + 1)), transpose to have samples as rows and genes as features.
4. Compute PCA using scikit-learn (`PCA`), extracting principal components and variance explained.
5. Generate a PCA scatter plot coloured by `condition` using matplotlib/seaborn and save to `results/pca_plot.png`.
6. Save sample PCA coordinates and variance explained to `results/pca_coordinates.csv`.

## Outputs
Types come from the closed vocabulary in _references/artifact_types.md.

| File | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| results/pca_plot.png | figure | PCA scatter plot of samples coloured by condition |
| results/pca_coordinates.csv | table | Principal component coordinates per sample |

## Execution
Runs: batch
Expected wall time: 5 minutes; expected output size: < 10MB.
